---
/**
 * The single inline script on the site.
 *
 * It has to be inline, and it has to run before anything paints: an external
 * script is fetched after first paint, so the page would render in the wrong
 * theme and then swap. That flash is the entire problem this solves.
 *
 * Because it is inline, the CSP allows it by SHA-256 hash rather than by
 * adding 'unsafe-inline'. The hash is computed in phase 10 from the *built*
 * HTML rather than from this source, so it is a hash of exactly the bytes that
 * get served — if Astro ever changes how it emits this, the hash follows.
 *
 * `is:inline` keeps Astro from bundling or transforming the contents, so what
 * is written here is what ships.
 *
 * The stored value is treated as untrusted: anything other than the two known
 * strings is ignored and the system preference wins. The localStorage read is
 * wrapped because it throws outright in Safari private mode rather than
 * returning null, and an exception here would block the rest of the page.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    try {
      var stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');
      if (stored === 'dark' || stored === 'light') {
        document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', stored);
      }
    } catch (error) {
      /* No storage access. The prefers-color-scheme media query still applies. */
    }
  })();
</script>
